From b3613ed8ff96a2da5afa808d8a4439594bc231ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:55:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: omap3isp: let the IOMMU idle while the ISP is not in
 use

The ISP attaches its IOMMU at probe, and omap-iommu keeps an attached
IOMMU enabled (a runtime PM reference from attach to detach). Its cam_ick
then never stops, the CAM power domain stays on, and cpuidle on OMAP3
uses only C1 while CAM is on ("CAM does not have wakeup capability"): on
the N950 the core never left ON and the MPU idled in C1 alone as soon as
the module was loaded, camera in use or not.

Drop the IOMMU's reference when the last ISP reference goes
(omap_iommu_domain_deactivate) and take it again with the first
(omap_iommu_domain_activate), as omap_remoteproc does around suspend.
Attach and detach both happen with the ISP held, so the references
balance: attach takes one, the final put of probe drops it, remove takes
it again before detaching.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/ti/omap3isp/isp.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/ti/omap3isp/isp.c b/drivers/media/platform/ti/omap3isp/isp.c
index f51cf6119..080cbf5b1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/ti/omap3isp/isp.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/ti/omap3isp/isp.c
@@ -1416,6 +1416,9 @@ static struct isp_device *__omap3isp_get(struct isp_device *isp, bool irq)
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	if (isp->mapping)
+		omap_iommu_domain_activate(isp->mapping->domain);
+
 	/* We don't want to restore context before saving it! */
 	if (isp->has_context)
 		isp_restore_ctx(isp);
@@ -1461,6 +1464,13 @@ static void __omap3isp_put(struct isp_device *isp, bool save_ctx)
 		if (!media_entity_enum_empty(&isp->crashed) ||
 		    isp->stop_failure)
 			isp_reset(isp);
+		/*
+		 * The IOMMU stays enabled for as long as it is attached, which
+		 * keeps cam_ick running and the CAM power domain on, and
+		 * cpuidle then never goes below C1. Let it idle with the ISP.
+		 */
+		if (isp->mapping)
+			omap_iommu_domain_deactivate(isp->mapping->domain);
 		isp_disable_clocks(isp);
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&isp->isp_mutex);
-- 
